  "worked_solution": "First, we complete a truth table for the part in parentheses, $B∨A.$  The statement $B∨A$ is true if either $A$ is true, $B$ is true, or both $A$ and $B$ are true.\n\n| $\\,A\\,$ | $\\,B\\,$ | $\\,B∨A\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n\nThen, we look at the columns labeled $A$ and $B∨A$ to complete the column $A∧(B∨A).$ The statement $A∧(B∨A)$ is true if both $A$ and $B∨A$ are true.\n\nThe completed truth table is shown below:\n\n| $\\,A\\,$ | $\\,B\\,$ | $\\,B∨A\\,$ | $\\,A∧(B∨A)\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ |",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
